pply patches according the following procedures:
Red Hat:
- For RAW servers change nunifixen010 in rhel-SLMA.repo to 167.104.10.118
- Add all servers into file with
- - servername O/S Hardware App
- - Use VMware as Hardware for VMs
- Run
- - Stage VMWare tools tar file on VMs
- - - StageVMwareTools.sh <filename>
- - Reset Web GUI for status
- - - ResetPatchWebGUI.sh <filename>
- - Disable patching
- - - DisablePaging.sh <filename>
- At time of patching run
- - StartPatchingAutoSrv.sh <filename>
- and in different window run
- - CheckServers.sh <filename>
- When everything is finished, run
- - CheckSrvAfterPatching.sh <filename>
HP/UX (there are no new patches for this O/S):
- Use Ignite to apply patches
- Parse through log-file and look for errors
Solaris:
- Copy recommended cluster to server (find large enough directory)
- Look for password in file for Solaris 10 servers
- Run script to apply recommended patches
- Parse through log-file and check for errors
